From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: finish stopping GPON LED blink before setting it

led_set_brightness(LED_OFF) schedules the software blink cancellation on
the LED workqueue. An immediate nonzero brightness call can still observe
LED_BLINK_SW and only update new_blink_brightness. The pending cancellation
then turns the LED off, losing the requested static-on state. On gpio-leds
the cached brightness can also retain the last blink phase after the worker
has driven the physical GPIO off.

The xPON LED helper already runs in sleepable context under led_lock. Flush
the LED work item after requesting blink cancellation, then apply the final
brightness. This makes both static-on and static-off deterministic and
updates their cached brightness after the blink timer has stopped.

Verified on XR500v v055 using a RAM observer: consumers resolved correctly
to green:pon/red:los and modes were ON/OFF, but both GPIOs were physically
off. Exercising blink followed by OFF, flush_work and final brightness
produced PON on/LOS off with matching cached values and no remaining blink.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -1206,8 +1206,10 @@ static void airoha_xpon_set_led(struct le
 {
 	if (!led || *current_mode == mode)
 		return;
-	if (*current_mode == AIROHA_XPON_LED_BLINK)
+	if (*current_mode == AIROHA_XPON_LED_BLINK) {
 		led_set_brightness(led, LED_OFF);
+		flush_work(&led->set_brightness_work);
+	}
 
 	switch (mode) {
 	case AIROHA_XPON_LED_ON:
